# Weights, engines and datasets are large and regenerable - keep them out of git.
# On the Jetson they live outside the repo (~/raptor-models, ~/raptor-data,
# ~/raptor-vlm, ~/raptor-deploy); these patterns stop a stray copy being committed.
#
# benchmarks/results/ and benchmarks/figures/ ARE committed: docs/06 calls the
# results the scientific output of the project, and a diff showing an FPS
# regression is exactly the feedback we want.
models/
videos/
data/
*.pt
*.engine
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.zip

# Ultralytics run artefacts
runs/

# Tooling
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets must never be committed. VNC/RDP passwords live only on the board
# (/etc/x11vnc.pass, grdctl's keyfile); these guard against a stray copy.
*.pass
*.key
*.pem
